WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.950
Overnight, SAM.gov becomes one list of decisions that need a person.

2
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.850
Every matching posting is scored against your company. Strong fits move on their own.

3
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.750
Score, deadline, and the next step. One screen.

4
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.650
What is blocked, what is waiting, and what only you can do.

5
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.550
Brost Co finds local trades and starts outreach before you sit down.

6
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:33.450
Email already ran. When a person is needed, the script is waiting.

7
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.350
Quotes land in one place. Missing trades stay visible until coverage is complete.

8
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:43.250
The package assembles as documents come in. Compliance checks run on their own.

9
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:48.150
You review and submit. Nothing goes out until you say so.

10
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:53.050
Today is waiting with the next human actions. The rest already ran.
